{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0c40d1f24190c39551ddf0eb50288376fb4e688991a5948ac280ddf563a1f0c2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A local-network collaboration feature shares loom sessions over WebSocket so team members can sync edits and model outputs without internet."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1aff519aae4c3939f1ef7a30b22f53aab0adc822cbaa6d4f0c5d110f2533646f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Inference runs via local backends including llama.cpp, ExLlama, and MLX, and models can be imported from Hugging Face, Ollama, or local GGUF/GPTQ files."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1f71f80423c143f50d67feb1216a3efc34453e6cfbfe1b8add349f0fc79d3414"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A 'loom' concept assigns a main 'warp' model for heavy tasks and auxiliary 'weft' models for fast tasks, with a cross-thread shuttle passing tokens between threads."},{"claim_ids":["clm_244f13b9d2eafcb0a93e09e9685de9f6edb0c1b608f1af51d9bcd9f6bdf14edd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is MIT-licensed, and a disclaimer notes that orchestrated models carry their own licenses and usage terms for which users are responsible."},{"claim_ids":["clm_32a706b7df033f96e32085a3c5c379ef89a7b6dcd4cdf236c9b3d20a2ce2b8df"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"CodeLoom is designed as an offline-only desktop tool that runs multiple open-source models locally with no cloud dependencies or data leaving the machine."},{"claim_ids":["clm_35c508f0a0ac363d91d79f270924eb2de42200a2c0f73dc8c1cd12c9d81d5a9a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Advanced users can write custom 'loom scripts' in Lua that define model interactions, thread switching, and output merging."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5c841f4ee2958fee2f9985721b5678c5ba1ab77cfcd5b8451699182023252f48"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The app indexes a codebase as context up to 100k tokens and splits it across model threads so each model sees a relevant slice."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9ee4ea1bd53bc51a05e76708d5c818440eab719c683f18c2618a5c63107bc042"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Stated system requirements: 16 GB RAM minimum (32 GB recommended), 6 GB VRAM minimum (12 GB+ recommended), 10 GB storage, on Windows 10, macOS 12+, or Linux kernel 5.x."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d6206c565ced58d367136d55323c4ceb868fff078f43f912fbc96d707a4d5259"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Per the FAQ, there is no cloud version by design, updates are manual downloads that only check a URL for version strings, and 7B models at 4-bit need at least 6 GB VRAM."},{"claim_ids":["clm_dc3d49f4d72e0242de79b014c31f7bc95b2f7ad73c8a491f7b2241555105694e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product supports up to five concurrent model sessions, each with its own context window, history, and parameters, and lets the user pick which thread's answer wins."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e23daa62e7c7ef158479c5e0c7640cd2454827c82c0006d018a3125029978433"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration is exposed through a loom_config.yaml file covering per-task model assignments, token budgets, sampling parameters, context-sharing rules, theme, and LAN-only remote access."},{"claim_ids":["clm_eede548c2c423cda8a9059c4286058050856f6a2402abcb014b28953613f2659"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Context can be merged between model threads manually or automatically, e.g. passing a small model's draft to a larger model without copy/paste."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0c40d1f24190c39551ddf0eb50288376fb4e688991a5948ac280ddf563a1f0c2","clm_1aff519aae4c3939f1ef7a30b22f53aab0adc822cbaa6d4f0c5d110f2533646f","clm_1f71f80423c143f50d67feb1216a3efc34453e6cfbfe1b8add349f0fc79d3414","clm_244f13b9d2eafcb0a93e09e9685de9f6edb0c1b608f1af51d9bcd9f6bdf14edd","clm_32a706b7df033f96e32085a3c5c379ef89a7b6dcd4cdf236c9b3d20a2ce2b8df","clm_35c508f0a0ac363d91d79f270924eb2de42200a2c0f73dc8c1cd12c9d81d5a9a","clm_5c841f4ee2958fee2f9985721b5678c5ba1ab77cfcd5b8451699182023252f48","clm_9ee4ea1bd53bc51a05e76708d5c818440eab719c683f18c2618a5c63107bc042","clm_d6206c565ced58d367136d55323c4ceb868fff078f43f912fbc96d707a4d5259","clm